v1.0.0
- Navigation listener registration now tracks successful attachments, cleans up partial registration, and rethrows failures instead of silently swallowing them; listener removal only runs for listeners that were actually attached.
- Consolidated detached runtime state into one shared S.O.P.H.I.A. object passed to the router; the voice engine is now router-owned instead of stored in a separate global.
- Five selectable companion voice packs: YES MAN, FISTO, KL-E-O, MK II Stealth Suit, and Andy / Mister Handy.
- Contextual companion voices across supported ITEMS, STATS, STATUS, and DATA menus.
- Smooth handoff when leaving the S.O.P.H.I.A. holotape or switching Pip-Boy sections.
- STATUS RAD remains silent and stops active S.O.P.H.I.A. speech while allowing normal STATUS navigation.
- Fallout 3 / Fallout: New Vegas mode-change companion responses in DATA > Settings.
- Detached low-memory router and transient voice-engine architecture.
- Readable source files with separate compact device runtime files.
